WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
An illustrated field guide connects CMC market data to the evidence behind each asset.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Explore declared custody and source documents. Regional statements remain attributed to
their sources.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Switch to sourced production figures. Country mine output is separate from token custody.

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Play the 2023–2025 production history. Units, source vintages and estimate flags stay
visible.

5
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Eleven dossiers now connect market observations to sources. This observed Top 10 includes
one partially documented asset.

6
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:44.000
STRCX tracks preferred stock. Select a relationship to inspect its source, date and legal
context; named custodians are not reserve-location pins.

7
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Compare six sourced relationships in the evidence matrix. Tokens referencing Circle can
have different issuers, instruments and rights.

8
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:58.000
USDon remains partially documented. Its settlement mechanism is sourced; legal issuer,
account-level custody and recovery rights remain unresolved.

9
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:04.000
The mobile layout keeps research status visible and makes the detailed evidence matrix
horizontally scrollable.

10
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Inspect the real API response: live keyed data, a complete category scan and dated
observations.
